{"name":"Ash Tree","hex":"#aabb99","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ash tree","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tree of the genus Fraxinus, with compound leaves and a tough, flexible wood."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ash_tree"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fraxinus","blocks":[{"text":"Fraxinus, commonly called ash, is a genus of plants in the olive and lilac family, Oleaceae, and comprises 45–65 species of usually medium-to-large trees, most of which are deciduous, although some subtropical species are evergreen. The genus is widespread throughout much of Europe, Asia, and North America."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Fraxinus_ornus_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-062.jpg/330px-Fraxinus_ornus_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-062.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fraxinus","wikidata":"Q128887"},{"title":"Ash","blocks":[{"text":"Ash is the solid remnants of fires. Specifically, ash refers to all non-aqueous, non-gaseous residues that remain after something burns. In analytical chemistry, to analyse the mineral and metal content of chemical samples, ash is the non-gaseous, non-liquid residue after complete combustion."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Wood_ash.jpg/330px-Wood_ash.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ash","wikidata":"Q152079"},{"title":"Tree","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, a tree is a perennial plant with an elongated stem, or trunk, usually supporting branches and leaves. In some usages, the definition of a tree may be narrower, e.g., including only woody plants with secondary growth, only plants that are usable for timber, or only plants above a specified height. Wider definitions include taller palms, tree ferns, bananas, and bamboos."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Usamljeni_jasen_-_panoramio_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Usamljeni_jasen_-_panoramio_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tree","wikidata":"Q10884"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Fraxinus_ornus_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-062.jpg/330px-Fraxinus_ornus_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-062.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Fraxinus_ornus_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-062.jpg/330px-Fraxinus_ornus_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-062.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKoeh-062.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/NarrowleafAsh.jpg/120px-NarrowleafAsh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/NarrowleafAsh.jpg/250px-NarrowleafAsh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/NarrowleafAsh.jpg/120px-NarrowleafAsh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANarrowleafAsh.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Ash_flower.JPG/120px-Ash_flower.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Ash_flower.JPG/250px-Ash_flower.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Ash_flower.JPG/120px-Ash_flower.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=